#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"icon:lock[title=Fixed at build time] [[quarkus-vertx_quarkus-vertx-native-transport-type]] [.property-path]##link:#quarkus-vertx_quarkus-vertx-native-transport-type[`+++quarkus.vertx.native-transport-type+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.vertx.native-transport-type+++[]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"The type of native transport to use.\n"
"\n"
"When set to a value other than `auto`, the application will attempt to use the specified native transport. If the transport is not available at runtime, the behavior depends on `native-transport()`.\n"
"\n"
"Setting this to a specific transport type implicitly enables native transport (i.e., `native-transport()` is treated as at least `if-available`).\n"
"\n"
"Supported values:\n"
"\n"
" * `auto` - Let Vert.x pick the best available transport (default)\n"
" * `epoll` - Use Linux epoll transport\n"
" * `kqueue` - Use macOS kqueue transport\n"
" * `io-uring` - Use Linux io_uring transport\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Note that, if not set to `auto`, Quarkus checks at build time that the requested transport type is available in the classpath. At runtime, it checks whether the transport can be used.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_VERTX_NATIVE_TRANSPORT_TYPE+++[]\n"
"--"
msgstr "[lock]  link:#quarkus-vertx_quarkus-vertx-native-transport-type[quarkus.vertx.native-transport-type] config_property_copy_button:quarkus.vertx.native-transport-type[]"

